    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling performance today, anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.49) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.01), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs above 4.30. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our primary engine today; his dynamic platoon advantage against Fisher provides a significant boost, making him a cornerstone for our production. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** (62.70) and **Heliot Ramos** (61.36) represent high-upside plays; **Sam Antonacci** capitalizes on a prime leadoff spot and a soft matchup against Melton, while **Heliot Ramos** benefits from a slow-delivering pitcher, increasing his probability of securing one of our coveted stolen bases. Despite a daunting 2.03 xERA matchup against Misiorowski, **Kyle Tucker** (54.15) remains in the lineup; while the SP skill penalty is severe, the combination of his talent and a favorable wind-out condition warrants the start over our deeper bench options.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer involved **Coby Mayo**, whose 44.18 score kept him on the fringe of our starting nine. Ultimately, **Coby Mayo** was held back by a difficult park factor and a low-velocity SP skill profile from Seymour, which depressed his baseline enough to favor the higher-rated **Miguel Vargas** and **Dominic Smith**. We remain cautious regarding several \"Lineup Pending\" designations\u2014specifically for **Drake Baldwin**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Jackson Merrill**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Wade Meckler**, and **Andy Pages**\u2014as late-scratch risks could force us to pivot toward depth. Furthermore, while **Gunnar Henderson** holds elite potential, the combination of a tough park and a negative platoon shift against Seymour makes him a high-risk play today, leaving him as our primary insurance policy on the bench.",
